{
  "description": "Secret redaction cases ported from the master test file. All credentials are fake test strings. `expect` holds only what the test asserts; `computed_result` is the full Python result (computed by running the extracted v2 module, identical to master). `computed_result.kinds` lists the placeholder kinds left in the output, in order, lowercased to the v3 kind names.",
  "source_file": "master:tests/unit/test_hooks_redaction.py",
  "function": "redact_secrets(text)",
  "expect_keys": {
    "contains": "each substring is in redacted_text",
    "not_contains": "no listed substring is in redacted_text",
    "contains_any": "at least one listed substring is in redacted_text",
    "redaction_count_min": "redaction_count >= value",
    "redaction_count": "redaction_count == value",
    "should_skip": "exact boolean",
    "redacted_text": "exact output"
  },
  "v3_note": "Python placeholders are `[REDACTED_<KIND>]`. For v3 (`[REDACTED:<kind>]`) substitute each `[REDACTED_<KIND>]` in contains/redacted_text with `[REDACTED:<kind lowercased>]`; `[REDACTED` prefixes in contains match both forms.",
